# Frontend

Phase 1 storefront lives in `frontend/`. Stack: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind.

- Keep `page.tsx` / layouts thin. Call application use cases, not fixture files or fetch/SQL.
- Prefer Server Components for crawlable catalog pages.
- Client Components only for interactive islands (cart, forms).
- Domain types must not import React or Next.js.
- Do not use `any` without a one-line justification. Prefer `unknown`.
- Do not call FastAPI until a Phase 2 task requires the HTTP repository.
- Semantic HTML: `header`, `main`, `footer`, headings in order, real links.

SEO is first-class: crawlable category/product HTML, metadata from data, canonicals, sitemap, robots, JSON-LD, OpenGraph, Next.js `Image`, internal links. Do not ship client-only catalog shells.

Cart in Phase 1 is client-side. Checkout must not charge cards in Phase 1.

Do not add dependencies unless the current task requires them. Do not create `package.json` during documentation-only tasks.
